      "page_title": "Async HTTP Fundamentals",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is async HTTP?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The coroutine sends a request, then ==awaits== the socket",
            "While it waits on I/O, the ==event loop== runs other coroutines",
            "Big win for I/O-bound fan-out: many requests, high latency",
            "**No** speedup for CPU-bound work: the loop is still one thread"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Coroutines and the loop",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def fetch(u): ...",
            "c = fetch(u)  # just an object",
            "await c       # now it runs",
            "asyncio.run(main())  # entry"
          ],
          "note": "calling does nothing until awaited or scheduled"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.run()` creates a fresh event loop",
            "Runs `main()` until it finishes",
            "**Cancels** any leftover tasks",
            "Closes the loop"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Sequential vs gather",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "for u in urls:",
            "    await fetch(u)  # one by one",
            "await asyncio.gather(",
            "    *(fetch(u) for u in urls))"
          ],
          "note": "only gather overlaps the waits"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Style",
            "3 reqs: 1s, 2s, 3s",
            "Total"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`for` + await",
              "sum",
              "6 s"
            ],
            [
              "`gather()`",
              "≈ slowest",
              "__3 s__"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "tasks = set()",
            "t = asyncio.create_task(fetch(u))",
            "tasks.add(t)  # strong ref",
            "t.add_done_callback(tasks.discard)"
          ],
          "note": "no reference, so the task can be GC'd mid-flight"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`requests.get()` inside async def: it's **blocking**",
            "The whole event loop freezes until it returns",
            "Calling `fetch()` without await: nothing is sent",
            "`create_task()` result dropped: the task can vanish"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. aiohttp vs httpx",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
