    {
      "page_title": "Client Lifecycle: Open, Use, Close",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is a client?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==ClientSession== holds the connector (pool), cookie jar and default headers",
            "Create one per **application**, never one per request",
            "`httpx.AsyncClient` works the same way: a pool plus shared config",
            "Set base_url, headers, auth and cookies **once** on the client"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Lifecycle mechanism",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Step",
            "aiohttp",
            "httpx"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Open",
              "`ClientSession()`",
              "`AsyncClient()`"
            ],
            [
              "Close",
              "`await s.close()`",
              "`await c.aclose()`"
            ],
            [
              "Auto-close",
              "`async with` exit",
              "`async with` exit"
            ],
            [
              "Body",
              "lazy: `await r.json()`",
              "**eager** unless streamed"
            ],
            [
              "Bad status",
              "ClientResponseError",
              "HTTPStatusError"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exiting `async with s.get(url) as r:` returns the conn to the **pool**",
            "Create the client inside running async code, where it binds to that ==event loop==",
            "Never share one client across loops or threads",
            "4xx/5xx don't raise on their own: call `r.raise_for_status()`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: aiohttp",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with ClientSession() as s:",
            "  async with s.get(url) as r:",
            "    r.raise_for_status()",
            "    data = await r.json()",
            "# session closed, conn released"
          ],
          "note": "exit the block to release the conn"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: httpx",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with httpx.AsyncClient(",
            "    base_url=API,",
            "    headers={'X-Key': KEY}) as c:",
            "  r = await c.get('/items')",
            "  r.raise_for_status()",
            "  items = r.json()  # no await"
          ],
          "note": "body already read, no await needed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Long-lived service",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@asynccontextmanager",
            "async def lifespan(app):",
            "  app.state.http = AsyncClient()",
            "  yield",
            "  await app.state.http.aclose()"
          ],
          "note": "open at startup, close on shutdown"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Top-level `httpx.get()` builds a throwaway client per call, so **no** pooling",
            "Session per request: fresh TCP + TLS every time, 1–3 extra RTTs",
            "Never closed: ==Unclosed client session== warning, leaked sockets",
            "Session built at import time, outside the running loop",
            "Assuming 4xx/5xx raise, when they return quietly"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "ClientSession & AsyncClient"
    },
