    {
      "page_title": "Connection Pooling and Limits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mechanism: keep-alive pool",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Keep-alive== reuses open TCP/TLS sockets per `(scheme, host, port)`",
            "Reuse **skips** the TCP + TLS handshakes (1-3 RTTs saved)",
            "Pool full → new request **queues** for a free socket",
            "aiohttp: that queue wait counts toward `connect` and `total` timeouts",
            "httpx: no socket frees in time → ==PoolTimeout=="
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Example: limit_per_host=2",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Event",
            "Socket",
            "Action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "req1 starts",
              "new #1",
              "handshake"
            ],
            [
              "req2 starts",
              "new #2",
              "handshake"
            ],
            [
              "req3 starts",
              "none free",
              "**queues**"
            ],
            [
              "req1 done",
              "#1 idle",
              "back to pool"
            ],
            [
              "req3 resumes",
              "reuse #1",
              "__no handshake__"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The knobs (defaults)",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "conn = aiohttp.TCPConnector(",
            "  limit=100,         # 0 = no cap",
            "  limit_per_host=0,  # 0 = no cap",
            "  ttl_dns_cache=10)  # DNS secs",
            "s = aiohttp.ClientSession(",
            "  connector=conn)"
          ],
          "note": "these values are the defaults"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`limit_per_host=10` caps sockets to **one** host, shielding that upstream",
            "`ttl_dns_cache=10`: resolved IPs cached 10 s",
            "`force_close=True` disables keep-alive → new socket per request"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "lim = httpx.Limits(",
            "  max_connections=100,",
            "  max_keepalive_connections=20,",
            "  keepalive_expiry=5.0)  # secs",
            "c = httpx.AsyncClient(",
            "  limits=lim, http2=True)"
          ],
          "note": "http2 needs pip install httpx[http2]"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`http2=True` ==multiplexes== many requests over one socket per host",
            "Only 20 idle sockets kept; each dropped after 5 s idle",
            "Pool wait bounded by `Timeout(pool=...)` → PoolTimeout"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. aiohttp vs httpx",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Knob",
            "aiohttp",
            "httpx"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Global cap",
              "`limit=100`",
              "`max_connections=100`"
            ],
            [
              "Per-host cap",
              "`limit_per_host`",
              "none (use HTTP/2)"
            ],
            [
              "Pool wait",
              "connect/total timeout",
              "`PoolTimeout`"
            ],
            [
              "No keep-alive",
              "`force_close=True`",
              "`max_keepalive_connections=0`"
            ],
            [
              "DNS cache",
              "`ttl_dns_cache=10`",
              "OS resolver"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Pool ≠ throttle",
          "text": "Pool limits cap ==sockets==; cap in-flight tasks with a Semaphore (p.5) and stop hangs with timeouts (p.4)."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same host → requests share ==one connection== as streams",
            "Falls back to HTTP/1.1 if the server lacks h2",
            "Still bound tasks: HTTP/2 doesn't limit memory"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "sockets, not tasks"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pool Leaks, Fixes & HTTP/2 Fan-out",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Mistakes that hang",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Response never read/released → socket **leaked**; pool drains, later requests hang",
            "Server closed idle socket → reuse fails `Server disconnected`",
            "Retry that error only for **idempotent** calls (GET/PUT/DELETE)",
            "`limit=10` caps sockets, not tasks: 10k tasks still created, just queue",
            "`force_close=True` \"to be safe\" → handshake on every call"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "r = await s.get(url)  # leak!",
            "if r.status != 200:",
            "    return None  # never released",
            "async with s.get(url) as r:",
            "    body = await r.read()",
            "# exit → socket back to pool"
          ],
          "note": "unreleased response pins its socket"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Symptom → fix",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Cause",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "later calls hang",
              "leaked responses",
              "`async with`"
            ],
            [
              "`PoolTimeout`",
              "pool too small",
              "raise limit / bound tasks"
            ],
            [
              "`Server disconnected`",
              "stale idle socket",
              "retry idempotent"
            ],
            [
              "slow every call",
              "`force_close=True`",
              "keep-alive on"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Example: HTTP/2 fan-out",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "c = httpx.AsyncClient(http2=True)",
            "rs = await asyncio.gather(",
            "  *(c.get(u) for u in urls))",
            "print(rs[0].http_version)"
          ],
          "note": "one socket per host, many streams"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Pool checklist",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set `limit_per_host` to what the upstream can take",
            "Release every response, even on error paths",
            "Keep-alive on; only `force_close` for broken servers",
            "Pair pool limits with a Semaphore and timeouts"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
