    {
      "page_title": "Per-Request and Total Timeouts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why timeouts",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No timeout → a ==stalled server== hangs the request **forever**",
            "Always set one; a hung await also holds a pool slot",
            "aiohttp default: `ClientTimeout(total=300, sock_connect=30)`",
            "That is 5 minutes, which is usually **far** too long"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. aiohttp ClientTimeout",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Bounds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`total`",
              "whole operation"
            ],
            [
              "`connect`",
              "pool wait + connect"
            ],
            [
              "`sock_connect`",
              "TCP connect"
            ],
            [
              "`sock_read`",
              "max gap between reads"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "from aiohttp import ClientTimeout",
            "t5 = ClientTimeout(total=5)",
            "async with s.get(url,",
            "        timeout=t5) as r:",
            "    data = await r.json()"
          ],
          "note": "per-request value overrides session default"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. httpx: per phase",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# default: 5s on EVERY phase",
            "t = httpx.Timeout(10.0,",
            "        connect=3.0)",
            "# read, write, pool → 10s",
            "c = httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=t)"
          ],
          "note": "phase limits, not a total deadline"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "aiohttp",
            "httpx"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Default",
              "300s total",
              "5s / phase"
            ],
            [
              "Model",
              "total + phases",
              "phases only"
            ],
            [
              "Total cap?",
              "yes (`total`)",
              "**no**"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Trickle trap",
          "text": "A server sends 1 byte every 4s. The httpx ==read timeout== (5s) never fires, so the request can run for **hours**."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Timeout exceptions",
          "items": [
            "aiohttp `total` → `asyncio.TimeoutError`",
            "aiohttp socket phases → `ServerTimeoutError`",
            "httpx: `ConnectTimeout`, `ReadTimeout`",
            "`WriteTimeout`, `PoolTimeout`, all subclasses of ==`TimeoutException`=="
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Hard overall deadline",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with asyncio.timeout(10):",
            "    rs = await asyncio.gather(",
            "        *(fetch(u) for u in us))",
            "# before 3.11:",
            "await asyncio.wait_for(coro, 10)"
          ],
          "note": "deadline cancels every gather child"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.timeout()` needs **3.11+**; otherwise use `wait_for`",
            "On the deadline, ==every child== request in gather() is cancelled",
            "The caller gets `TimeoutError`, whatever the phase limits say"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`timeout=None` in httpx disables **all** timeouts → silent hang",
            "Trusting aiohttp's 300s default in production",
            "Treating httpx's read timeout as a total cap",
            "Deadline only on sockets and none on the caller"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Keep **connect** short (3–5s), match ==read== to the endpoint's SLA, and put a __total deadline__ on the caller."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "never wait forever"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Bounded Concurrency",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why unbounded gather hurts",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "gather() over ==10,000 URLs== starts **10,000** tasks at once",
            "Memory spikes: every task and buffer is live together",
            "Long pool queues and file-descriptor exhaustion",
            "Upstream answers with {red:429 Too Many Requests}"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Semaphore: at most n",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
